Team,

Before this becomes another standing report, can we answer the real question?

During service degradation, repeated attempts can inflate volume and obscure =
the number of customers actually affected. The possible stories are that chan=
nel switching follows a timeout, that customers retry the same action within =
minutes, or that automatic retry and human retry are being mixed.

This has returned because the previous answer was useful but not strong enoug=
h to become a standing rule. Use July 2024 as the new evidence point rather t=
han recycling the earlier conclusion. Please start with the decision we need =
to make, then show whether the available evidence is strong enough to support=
 it.

Please prepare a one-page finding note plus the underlying CSV for our own re=
view. The output must help us decide how monitoring should count affected cus=
tomers and when retry controls should activate.

Data available: transaction-level timestamps, channels, amounts, statuses and=
 error context; ATM attempts, host responses, PIN attempts, blocked-card stat=
e and latency.

Please state the limitation plainly: Without application session IDs, use acc=
ount, amount, channel and time proximity as an explicit matching heuristic.

